    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"currency - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\":\n    \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/currency.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [currency()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\n    | EdgeCase\n  description: Exchange rates between six currencies, with one arbitrage loop.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [currency()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\n    | EdgeCase\n  description: Exchange rates between six currencies, with one arbitrage loop.\ntitle: >-\n  [currency()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Exchange rates between six currencies, with one arbitrage loop.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nExchange rates between six currencies, with one arbitrage loop.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/example_networks.py#L1177-L1289){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\ncurrency(arbitrage=True)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\nThe rates quoted one afternoon at a made-up currency desk, for the shortest-path methods\nthat allow negative weights. Each edge is a quote, directed from the currency sold to the\ncurrency bought, and its `rate` is how many units of the second one unit of the first buys.\nConverting along a path multiplies the rates, so the edges are weighted by the negative\nlogarithm of the rate: the path of least total weight is the best way to convert, and a\nrate above 1 is a negative weight. A cycle of negative total weight is an arbitrage: a\nround trip that ends with more money than it started with. The euro–pound quotes are out\nof date and make one such loop; set `arbitrage=False` to correct them.\n\nNetwork Properties:\n\n- 6 nodes (currencies, labeled by ISO code, such as `\"USD\"`)\n- 18 edges (9 traded pairs, each quoted both ways)\n- Directed, weighted by the negative log of the rate, with negative weights\n- Strongly connected\n\nNode Attributes:\n\n- `name`: the currency's name, such as `\"Swiss franc\"`\n\nEdge Attributes:\n\n- `rate`: the units of the target currency bought by one unit of the source currency\n- `neg_log_rate`: $-\\ln(\\text{rate})$, the same as the edge weight\n\nWhat to Look For:\n\n- **One arbitrage loop.** Dollars changed to euros, then pounds, then back to dollars,\n  return 1.00099 dollars for each dollar: the only cycle of negative total weight. Every\n  other round trip loses money to the spreads.\n- **Negative weights.** Every rate above 1 (a pound buys 1.26873 dollars) is a negative\n  weight, so Dijkstra's algorithm doesn't apply; Bellman-Ford, Johnson and Goldberg-Radzik\n  do, once `arbitrage=False` removes the loop.\n- **The direct route isn't the best.** Few people trade yen for Swiss francs, so the direct\n  quote loses 0.5% to the spread, while going through the dollar loses 0.2%.\n- **A hub and a spoke.** The dollar trades against every other currency, and the Canadian\n  dollar against the US dollar only, so every route to or from it goes through `\"USD\"`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[arbitrage]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Whether the euro–pound quotes are the stale ones that make the arbitrage loop. Default is\n    `True`. With `False`, they're corrected and no cycle has negative total weight.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The exchange-rate network.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nSome cycle has negative total weight, and the one reachable from the dollar is the\narbitrage loop:\n\n::: {#dc0541ed .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nfx = ec.currency()\nloop = fx.find_negative_cycle(\"USD\")\n\nfx.negative_edge_cycle(), [fx.get_label_from_id(n) for n in loop]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(True, ['EUR', 'GBP', 'USD', 'EUR'])\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nMultiplying the rates around the loop gives the gain on each unit of currency, and\ndrawing the loop's quotes highlighted shows where it runs:\n\n::: {#987f128c .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport math\n\nedges = fx.get_edge_df()\npairs = list(zip(edges[\"source\"], edges[\"target\"]))\nrate = dict(zip(pairs, edges[\"rate\"]))\nedge_id = dict(zip(pairs, edges[\"id\"]))\n\nsteps = list(zip(loop, loop[1:]))\nround(math.prod(rate[step] for step in steps), 5)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n1.00099\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#44555e0d .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfx.plot(\n    highlight_edges=[edge_id[step] for step in steps],\n    label_by=\"label\", curved_edges=True, seed=4,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"5.6 14.0 688.8 492.0\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"5.6\" y=\"14.0\" width=\"688.8\" height=\"492.0\" fill=\"var(--ect-323